NUM-43: clamp the cosine of the sunset hour angle in getTempEvap()

getTempEvap() took acos(-tan(lat)*tan(decl)) without a range check. Above
the polar circles the argument leaves [-1, 1] around the solstices, acos()
returns NaN, and the Hargreaves evaporation rate, the runoff balance and the
subcatchment storage all become NaN. Limit the argument to [-1, 1] (hour
angle pi when the sun never sets, 0 when it never rises), as
updateTempTimes() in the same file already does. Results at latitudes
where the argument stays in range are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-43_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/climate.c b/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
index c343b93..5732a65 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
@@ -1352,7 +1352,9 @@ double getTempEvap(int day, double tave, double trng)
     double dr = 1.0 + 0.033 * cos(a * day);              // relative earth-sun distance
     double phi = Temp.anglat * 2.0 * PI / 360.0;         // latitude angle (rad)
     double del = 0.4093 * sin(a * (284. + (double)day)); // solar declination angle (rad)
-    double omega = acos(-tan(phi) * tan(del));           // sunset hour angle (rad)
+    double x = MAX(-1.0, MIN(1.0, -tan(phi) * tan(del))); // cos(omega), kept in [-1, 1]
+                                                         // in polar day and night
+    double omega = acos(x);                              // sunset hour angle (rad)
     double ra = 37.6 * dr *                              // extraterrestrial radiation
                 (omega * sin(phi) * sin(del) +
                  cos(phi) * cos(del) * sin(omega));
